{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-37683" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{x}^{1/x}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,dy\\,dx.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec45a64112d79e9fd8354ff1ec2bd21340193ef409d3cef71b7b2f170797ee91"} {"question" "q-37683" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{x}^{1/x}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}[{\\int }_{x}^{1/x}y\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{x}^{1/x}dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}-{x}^{2})dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}-1)\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}-1)\\,dx & =\\frac{1}{2}{[-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}}-x]}_{1/2}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}[\\frac{1}{3}+1-(\\frac{8}{3}+\\frac{1}{2})] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{11}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec45a64112d79e9fd8354ff1ec2bd21340193ef409d3cef71b7b2f170797ee91"} {"question" "q-37683" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "00e7898d1597c2bacc28705c208413b6b90b364221cc0224ef6803f23768565b"} {"question" "q-37683" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec45a64112d79e9fd8354ff1ec2bd21340193ef409d3cef71b7b2f170797ee91"} {"question" "q-37683" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{11}{4}"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{11}"] ["math" "\\frac{11}{12}"] ["math" "\\frac{11}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{6}{11}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec45a64112d79e9fd8354ff1ec2bd21340193ef409d3cef71b7b2f170797ee91"} {"question" "q-37683" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{11}{12}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec45a64112d79e9fd8354ff1ec2bd21340193ef409d3cef71b7b2f170797ee91"} {"question" "q-37865" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the double integral\n${∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{(1+x+y)^{2}}\\,dA,$\nwhere $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the line\n$y=1-x$ and the coordinate axes." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec45a64112d79e9fd8354ff1ec2bd21340193ef409d3cef71b7b2f170797ee91"} {"question" "q-37865" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's make a sketch of our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/assets/95ebd0a4eb874972b459e53eecf1d57650f63284698fcad967c09620ac01cd99.png)\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I region.\n\n- The line $y=1-x$ intercepts the $x$-axis at $x=1.$\nSo, the $x$-limits are \n$0\\le x\\le 1.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/assets/d048f20f2299722cee598cc1005237627ecdd7643e996b269f26b5a096f01f2f.png)\n\nAs a result, the integral is defined over the following type I region: \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1-x}\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{(1+x+y)^{2}}\\,dA={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}\\frac{1}{(1+x+y)^{2}}\\,dy\\,dx\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}\\frac{1}{(1+x+y)^{2}}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{-x+1}\\frac{1}{(1+x+y)^{2}}\\,dy]\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[-\\frac{1}{1+x+y}]}_{0}^{-x+1}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-\\frac{1}{1+x+(1-x)}-(-\\frac{1}{1+x+0}))\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{1+x})dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{1+x})dx & ={[-\\frac{1}{2}x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x)]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-(0+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec45a64112d79e9fd8354ff1ec2bd21340193ef409d3cef71b7b2f170797ee91"} {"question" "q-37865" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "00e7898d1597c2bacc28705c208413b6b90b364221cc0224ef6803f23768565b"} {"question" "q-37865" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec45a64112d79e9fd8354ff1ec2bd21340193ef409d3cef71b7b2f170797ee91"} {"question" "q-37865" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+\\frac{1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec45a64112d79e9fd8354ff1ec2bd21340193ef409d3cef71b7b2f170797ee91"} {"question" "q-37865" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec45a64112d79e9fd8354ff1ec2bd21340193ef409d3cef71b7b2f170797ee91"} {"question" "q-40747" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/assets/ce364dc7c6c4fc5e229fdeb0809b3779bf1052c60d956deb742731f34e54562d.png)\n\nIf $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the lines $y=2x,$ $x=0,$ and $y=4,$ as shown above, then ${∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\sqrt{x}\\,dA=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec45a64112d79e9fd8354ff1ec2bd21340193ef409d3cef71b7b2f170797ee91"} {"question" "q-40747" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. \n\n- To determine the $x$-limits, we need to find the $x$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =4 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $x$-limits are \n$0\\le x\\le 2.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/assets/54f366679684823341bab818459ce5fc884ebbdd2376e800b781d1b832c4ba64.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,2x\\le y\\le 4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2x}^{4}{y}^{2}\\sqrt{x}\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec45a64112d79e9fd8354ff1ec2bd21340193ef409d3cef71b7b2f170797ee91"} {"question" "q-40747" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "00e7898d1597c2bacc28705c208413b6b90b364221cc0224ef6803f23768565b"} {"question" "q-40747" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec45a64112d79e9fd8354ff1ec2bd21340193ef409d3cef71b7b2f170797ee91"} {"question" "q-40747" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-2x}^{4}{y}^{2}\\sqrt{x}\\,dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2x}^{4}{y}^{2}\\sqrt{x}\\,dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{4}^{2x}{y}^{2}\\sqrt{x}\\,dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x/2}^{4}{y}^{2}\\sqrt{x}\\,dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x}^{4}{y}^{2}\\sqrt{x}\\,dy\\,dx"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec45a64112d79e9fd8354ff1ec2bd21340193ef409d3cef71b7b2f170797ee91"} {"question" "q-40747" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2x}^{4}{y}^{2}\\sqrt{x}\\,dy\\,dx"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec45a64112d79e9fd8354ff1ec2bd21340193ef409d3cef71b7b2f170797ee91"} {"question" "q-81776" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/assets/6accbfcccdf910acca3aab9f1a12d0ab35c4da683fe78d6ca2d7ada88f28767c.png)\n\nEvaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\,dA,$\nwhere $D$ is the finite region above the $x$-axis enclosed by the curve $y=1-{x}^{2}$ and the line $x=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec45a64112d79e9fd8354ff1ec2bd21340193ef409d3cef71b7b2f170797ee91"} {"question" "q-81776" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $D$ is a type I region.\n\n- We already know the intersection of the curve with the line $y=0.$\nSo, the $x$-limits are \n$0\\le x\\le 1.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/assets/db0dd47348fb2f9a97c9e0514f74adae05830de7e03f1aea2886eaa95701200e.png)\n\nAs a result, the integral is defined over the following type I region: \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1-{x}^{2}}\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\,dA={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}{x}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}{x}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}[y]_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}(1-{x}^{2}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}-{x}^{4})\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}-{x}^{4})\\,dx & ={[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{5}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec45a64112d79e9fd8354ff1ec2bd21340193ef409d3cef71b7b2f170797ee91"} {"question" "q-81776" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "00e7898d1597c2bacc28705c208413b6b90b364221cc0224ef6803f23768565b"} {"question" "q-81776" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec45a64112d79e9fd8354ff1ec2bd21340193ef409d3cef71b7b2f170797ee91"} {"question" "q-81776" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "15"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{15}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{7}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec45a64112d79e9fd8354ff1ec2bd21340193ef409d3cef71b7b2f170797ee91"} {"question" "q-81776" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{15}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec45a64112d79e9fd8354ff1ec2bd21340193ef409d3cef71b7b2f170797ee91"} {"question" "q-132276" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,dy\\,dx=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec45a64112d79e9fd8354ff1ec2bd21340193ef409d3cef71b7b2f170797ee91"} {"question" "q-132276" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x[\\,y\\,]_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,dx & ={[-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(-2) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec45a64112d79e9fd8354ff1ec2bd21340193ef409d3cef71b7b2f170797ee91"} {"question" "q-132276" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "00e7898d1597c2bacc28705c208413b6b90b364221cc0224ef6803f23768565b"} {"question" "q-132276" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec45a64112d79e9fd8354ff1ec2bd21340193ef409d3cef71b7b2f170797ee91"} {"question" "q-132276" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec45a64112d79e9fd8354ff1ec2bd21340193ef409d3cef71b7b2f170797ee91"} {"question" "q-132276" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067291/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec45a64112d79e9fd8354ff1ec2bd21340193ef409d3cef71b7b2f170797ee91"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2245 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
